## Step 2 — Measures to Create

There are **two measure patterns** depending on topic. Both go on `fact_acs_wi_county`.

---

### Pattern A — Demographics (dynamic filter, no SWITCH needed)

These measures ignore the `Measure Name` column entirely. They read the selected Indicator and Demographic directly from the cascade slicers and filter `dim_dem_category` using TREATAS.

**`Selected Geography Female`** (create on `fact_acs_wi_county`, format: Auto)

```
Selected Geography Female =
VAR Topic       = SELECTEDVALUE(dim_geography_categories[Topic])
VAR Indicator   = SELECTEDVALUE(dim_geography_categories[Indicator])
VAR Group       = SELECTEDVALUE(dim_geography_categories[Demographic])
VAR MeasureName = SELECTEDVALUE(dim_geography_categories[Measure Name])
RETURN
IF(
    Topic = "Demographics",
    CALCULATE(
        [Selected Demo Breakdown Female],
        TREATAS({ Group },      dim_dem_category[group_label]),
        TREATAS({ Indicator },  dim_dem_category[category_type])
    ),
    SWITCH(
        MeasureName,
        "Total Births WI",              [Total Births WI],
        "Teen Birth Count",             [Teen Birth Count],
        "Female Victim Count",          [Female Victim Count],
        "Assault Female Victims",       [Assault Female Victims],
        "Sex Offense Female Victims",   [Sex Offense Female Victims],
        "Homicide Female Victims",      [Homicide Female Victims],
        "Median Earnings All Female",   [Median Earnings All Female],
        "Median Earnings Mgmt Female",  [Median Earnings Mgmt Female],
        "Median Earnings Service Female",[Median Earnings Service Female],
        "Median Earnings Sales Female", [Median Earnings Sales Female],
        "Median Earnings NRC Female",   [Median Earnings NRC Female],
        "Median Earnings Prod Female",  [Median Earnings Prod Female],
        BLANK()
    )
)
```

> ⚠️ `dim_dem_category[category_type]` — verify this is the actual column name in your table that holds values like "Age", "Race", "Education", "Marital Status". Update the column name if it differs.

