## Step 3 — Page Layout

### Three cascade slicers (all from `dim_geography_categories`)
| Slicer | Field | Style |
|---|---|---|
| 1 — Topic | `dim_geography_categories[Topic]` | Tile, Single select |
| 2 — Indicator | `dim_geography_categories[Indicator]` | Dropdown, Single select |
| 3 — Demographic | `dim_geography_categories[Demographic]` | Dropdown, Single select |

Single-table cascade: selecting "Crime and Violence" in Slicer 1 automatically limits Slicer 2 to Assault/Homicide/Sex Offenses/Victims/Offenders, and so on. No DAX needed.

### Two filled maps
| Visual | Field — Location | Field — Values |
|---|---|---|
| Female map | `dim_geography[County Name]` | `Selected Geography Female` |
| Male map | `dim_geography[County Name]` | `Selected Geography Male` |

### No relationships needed
`dim_geography_categories` is disconnected. The two SWITCH measures read it via SELECTEDVALUE(). The existing `dim_geography → fact_acs_wi_county` relationship handles county filtering on the maps.

